# MYSTIC LINT / FORMAT / TEST AFTER EVERY FILE CHANGE

After **every** file edit, update, addition, or deletion in `/home/mystic/mystic` (Local Cursor VM), agents MUST run this exact chain from the repo root before considering the work done:

```bash
cd /home/mystic/mystic
./venv/bin/ruff check . --fix && ./venv/bin/ruff format . && ./venv/bin/pytest
```

## When this applies

- Any create, edit, or delete of a tracked or new file under the Mystic repo
- Code, tests, config, scripts, and docs
- Multiple files in one turn: run the chain **once at the end**, after the last edit
- If a fix is required to make ruff or pytest pass, apply it, then **re-run the full chain**

## Tools

- Use the project venv binaries: `/home/mystic/mystic/venv/bin/ruff` and `/home/mystic/mystic/venv/bin/pytest`
- Do not use a different ruff or a system pytest

## Do not skip

- Do not skip because the change "looks small"
- Do not skip because only comments, docs, or config changed
- Do not skip because ruff/pytest ran earlier in the same session
- If the user asked for read-only research / no code changes, do **not** edit files and do **not** run `--fix` (no files were changed)

## Failure handling

- If `ruff check . --fix` reports remaining errors, fix them and re-run the full chain
- If `pytest` fails, fix the failure and re-run the full chain
- Do not declare the edit complete while the chain is red

## Exceptions

- User explicitly said not to lint/format/test
- User explicitly requested read-only / no code changes
- The only action was a git commit/push with no file content edits in that turn
